laurel (Mi A3, iOS 26): the resident set: with a kernel that answers GET_PARAM 0x7c = 1 (RedwoodGPU laurel 3060) a submission is flagged MSM_SUBMIT_LAUREL_RESIDENT and lists its command buffers only (each once); the kernel takes every live buffer of the client as named. Before, the device's whole list went in at every submission (about 2,500 buffers with live glass: a 40 KiB copyin and three kernel walks each). One line LAUREL TURNIP RESIDENT: on|off (the kernel's answer is the self-check). Kill switch NEGRONIMETAL_RESIDENT=0. Host: ios26-encode-bench.sh with IOCTL_COUNT_RESIDENT=1 (ioctl-count.so answers the param) runs the on path on Mesa's drm-shim.

